Test stanzas in order of test name (gh-ocannl-2193): below a dune file's marker comment a
stanza sits where its test's name sorts, and every aggregate alias lists its members in
order, so two branches that each add a test meet only when the names are neighbours. The
counts go to stderr, since a tally in a golden moves with every test.

every file that must carry the marker was handed to the scan: true
the ordered part the scan read holds hundreds of stanzas, so the order claim is not vacuous: true
no stanza is out of place and no aggregate alias lists its members out of order: true

Controls, on files built to be refused:
a file whose tests are in order of name is accepted: true
a test appended at the end of the file is refused, with the place it belongs: true
the same test in its place is accepted: true
a test's executable, its variant rules and its golden diffs are one group, in any order: true
a rule sorts under its per-test alias, so one filed under another test's name is refused: true
stanzas above the marker are not ordered: true
a stanza below the marker that names no test is refused: true
an aggregate alias whose members are out of order is refused, above the marker too: true
an aggregate alias listing a member twice is refused: true
a file without the marker is left alone: true
a file that must carry the marker and does not is refused: true
a file carrying the marker twice is refused: true
a key is cut at its first `-` or `.`, and at nothing else: true

